# scripts/check.conf — the steps behind the single verification contract (./scripts/check).
# Generated by the bootstrap workflow; this example shows the format.
# One step per line:  <name>: <command>   — runs in order, fails fast.
# Every command must leave nothing running (docs/testing.md, Resource hygiene).
# Tag quick steps with [fast] in the NAME (never in the command): ./scripts/check --fast runs only
# those; ./scripts/check runs all (docs/testing.md, Two speeds, one contract).
#
# Prerequisites:  requires <step name>: <command>   — the step name as shown, without [fast].
# A command you write that exits 0 when this machine can run the step; side-effect free, quick,
# starts nothing. check runs them before the first step (unmet → red, environment gap R-13);
# doctor reports which profile this machine can run. ANEW knows no tool: you name what you use.
# requires test: node -e "process.exit(+process.versions.node.split('.')[0] >= 20 ? 0 : 1)"
# A step that needs a container runtime names the one the project uses, e.g. one of:
# requires integration: docker info
# requires integration: podman info
#
# JVM (Gradle, Java) example:
# resource hygiene: no Gradle daemon
# build [fast]: ./gradlew assemble --no-daemon
# test: ./gradlew test --no-daemon
#
# Node example:
# lint: npm run lint
# typecheck: npm run typecheck
# test: npm test
#
# Python example:
# lint: ruff check .
# types: mypy .
# test: pytest -q
